  "followup_on_nov20_entries": {
    "2091b351": "Candidate and main already share the theme-aware BaseKeyboard Return implementation. ExpandedCandidateLayout Keyboard still overrides it with a raw resource. The upstream deletion can be isolated with the four existing icon tests, covering SVG/font/resource, composing and editor-action icons, reopen and Gboard fallbacks. Not adopted in this run.",
    "02da5cbe": "ThemePrefs projects independently saved main and non-main opacity onto one key_opacity by preferring main when it is non-100, multiplies a separate glass opacity if enabled, and removes wallpaper blend control. A single scalar cannot retain separate non-default values. Adapt as an optional glass effect without discarding useful existing controls or settings. Review also KeyView overlay geometry and RTL window capability.",
    "a57a0a10": "Adds the existing keyboard test menu on the theme appearance page. The entry itself may be isolated from glass migration. Reuse existing group navigation and personal UI terms.",
    "54f5e2b8": "Separates preedit presence from candidates-only compose state via a new hasPreedit parameter and forces refresh on returning to the keyboard. Valid for Compact18 only after merge with action-based personal Shift and tests for repeated empty notifications.",
    "ce5d670f": "Adds Return/Keypad Enter pinyin highlight synchronization for hardware and virtual key paths before native sendKey. Preserve personal optional takeovers and verify first-page/docked/floating native indices across render changes and page moves. Native raw-code commit changes decided jointly with d56562e2.",
    "6a9088c9/20a45f2e": "Adds opt-in status toolbar layout/profile entry points, then moves profile choice into an IME window. The second patch suppresses layout-source change notification during previews and adds explicit lazy-cache/active layout refresh. Check stale previews, split/theme configuration, explicit selection, attached editor and file watchers together.",
    "c9925d47": "Resettable preference classes move packages. Android restores dialogs from class names; MainActivity installs a FragmentFactory before super.onCreate to recognize two old names. Verify actual rotation/process restore and any saved dialog tags; keep keys and search destinations.",
    "c5b41188/d56562e2": "Fetched Chinese-addons pins bc96a64d..053fd54d and e8cb6b36..4bcc1c2d. The first rewires decoded raw commit and highlight behavior. The latter applies typed key commit to full 26-key mode while preserving compact and Shift+Return, including explicit separator and full pinyin display cases.",
    "26e0d48c": "Fetched corresponding Chinese-addons and libime ranges. e8cb6b36 includes nearby-key correction and viewport-sensitive placement/forgetting. libime 1511c085 marks grouped layouts and changes first-letter matching; fcitx pin e18d4bf3 brings fallback candidate metadata. Integrate as one protocol batch after learning/history, candidate and compact layout tests.",
    "40bc3031": "Android tests pin final-syllable completion and post-selection prefix behavior across threshold values. Native libime 1ada6bda changes pinyin context/encoder/IME plus regression tests. Existing PartialSp and per-IM saved configurations still need an integration path.",
    "b21b228f": "Upstream fixture stops the daemon, isolates only two learned correction files, backs up/restores contents and restarts in finally. Run on disposable Android storage, avoid fixed candidate ranks, and verify absent source files stay absent after test.",
    "55c53bcc": "Uses a scrollable material chip grid only for compact group presets and symbol selection, retaining original indexes and text. Reuse accessible labels and saved key schema. Depends on the compact editor.",
    "4f1db725/3ee4e9f3": "Free regrouping, thresholds and compact-only detection span custom layout validation, JNI group synchronization and fuzzy settings. Verify no loss of custom entries/26-key behavior, and keep explicit fuzzy preferences while switching layouts."
  },
